{"reference":"Ezekiel 9","book":"Ezekiel","chapter":9,"status":"pending","sections":[{"kind":"interpretive_questions","title":"The Movement of God's Glory","blocks":[{"id":"block_1","text":"The movement of the glory of the God of Israel in verse 3 belongs to a larger vision spanning chapters 8–11, in which that glory moves from the defiled Jerusalem temple and city. The vision later depicts its return to the visionary sanctuary in chapter 43.","verse_refs":["Ezekiel 9:1-11"],"provenance_refs":["reader_path_ezekiel_009_2bdfe797375cda41f07b554e"],"confidence":"high","interpretation_level":"disputed"}]}],"generated_metadata":null}